  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc164105 and CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of molecular interactions involving Leukocyte antigen CD37. The core mechanism appears to be the targeting of CD37 by two distinct compounds: 5,7-Dihydroxy-3-[3-hydroxy-4-methoxy-5-(3-methylbut-2-enyl)phenyl]chromen-4-one and (A+/-)-1,3,3-Trimethyl-2-norbornanol. Both compounds are identified as targets of Npc164105, and their interaction with CCRF-HSB-2 is supported by the final scores in the datasets. The presence of two distinct ligands targeting the same target suggests a possible dual mechanism, though the exact role of each compound in the pathway remains to be elucidated. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance and specificity of the interactions.",
